# SPA fallback: serve index.html for all routes that don't match a static file.
# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the build output directory.
#
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# CAUTION: redirect rules run BEFORE static assets are served, so never add a
# rule for a path the prerenderer writes real HTML to (/CaseStudy/:slug and
# every route in scripts/prerender.mjs) — the rule would shadow the static
# file. Only retired legacy paths belong here.

# Unsubscribe links in outreach email point at c4studios.com.au rather than a
# supabase.co URL: recipients (and school mail filters) trust the known domain.
# The function opts them out, then redirects to /unsubscribed, which IS
# prerendered — hence the path here is /unsubscribe/*, not /unsubscribed/*.
#
# The token MUST stay in the destination path. Cloudflare Pages does not
# substitute :splat inside a destination query string: `?u=:splat` forwarded the
# literal "%3Asplat" and every emailed link died on badlink. Verified 12 Aug.
/unsubscribe/*  https://hauwhplevypinplfbbgh.supabase.co/functions/v1/unsubscribe/:splat  302

